{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/anthropics/claude-code/main/config-schema.json",
  "_comment": [
    "Personal overrides — copy to settings.local.json (gitignored).",
    "NOTE: install.sh provisions live defaults from settings.local.json.default; this .example is the full documented toggle reference (not the install source).",
    "Scalars override settings.json values; arrays merge; deny wins over allow.",
    "Common use cases:",
    "  - Add project-specific permissions (docker, kubectl, etc.)",
    "  - Set environment variables (GIT_STRIP_CO_AUTHOR, etc.)",
    "  - Override model for local development",
    "  - Configure worktree.sparsePaths for monorepo optimization"
  ],
  "_env_comment": [
    "Within the `env` block below, keys with a leading '_' are inactive — remove the underscore prefix to activate them. (Top-level `_comment` / `_env_comment` / `_worktree_comment` are documentation keys, not env vars.)",
    "CLAUDE_HANDOFF_VALIDATION_MODE   (IMP-01) warn|strict — strict blocks writes of invalid handoff JSON",
    "CLAUDE_VERDICT_VALIDATION_MODE   (IMP-02) warn|strict — strict forces VERDICT_JSON schema pass (falls back to regex otherwise)",
    "CLAUDE_ISSUE_ID_VALIDATION_MODE  (IMP-03) warn|strict — strict blocks verdict records whose issues[].id fails the canonical pattern ^[PC]R-[0-9a-f]{8}$. Default: warn (regex fallback still rescues the verdict; logs to workflow-state/handoff-validation.jsonl).",
    "CLAUDE_PROJECT_KNOWLEDGE_MODE    (planner-genericity) warn|strict — strict BLOCKS /workflow startup when PROJECT-KNOWLEDGE.md is missing or contains placeholder values for M+ complexity tasks. Default: warn (one-line stderr message, non-blocking).",
    "CLAUDE_PK_PATH_MODE              (meta-agent/check-references) warn|strict — strict makes bare PROJECT-KNOWLEDGE.md reference detection (without .claude/ prefix) BLOCK the write (exit 2). Default: warn (stdout message, non-blocking).",
    "All envs are independent. Default: warn on all. Set to strict for full enforcement.",
    "ENABLE_PROMPT_CACHING_1H  (v2.1.108) — 1H TTL for API-key/Bedrock/Vertex/Foundry (2× write cost; noop for subscription users). See CLAUDE.md > Prompt Cache Policy.",
    "FORCE_PROMPT_CACHING_5M   (v2.1.108) — force 5-min TTL regardless of tier (cost control for S/M tasks)",
    "CLAUDE_DELTA_REVIEW_MODE    (delta-review-mode) off|warn|strict — off=disabled (default, byte-identical, zero behavioral change). warn=HINT advisory delta-focus for iter >=2 reviewers (plan: Part list; code: file list via git diff). strict=FOCUS narrower scope (opt-in indefinitely, no planned default flip).",
    "CLAUDE_CAVEMAN_MODE         (caveman) lite|off — lite (default if hook present and var unset) activates project-local caveman terse-output mode for /workflow parent session (orchestrator/designer/planner/coder). off disables caveman entirely; reviewer/researcher agents are exempt regardless via SubagentStart suspend hook. Resolution: env > .claude/workflow-state/.caveman-mode flag > 'lite'.",
    "CLAUDE_ISSUE_ID_NORMALIZE_VERSION (P2) 2|1 — 2 (default) applies NFKC + strip + collapse-whitespace + lowercase + strip-terminal-punctuation before sha256 in save-review-checkpoint.sh::_compute_canonical_id. 1 reverts to raw v1 hashing for forensic re-run of pre-2026-05-02 canonical IDs.",
    "CLAUDE_VERDICT_BLOCK_TTL_HOURS (P3) integer hours — TTL for .verdict-block-{agent_id} sentinels. Default 6. Setting 0 disables eviction (pre-Part-4 never-evict behaviour). Eviction runs at the entry of inject-review-context.sh and save-review-checkpoint.sh; counter verdict_blocks_evicted appended to pipeline-metrics.jsonl.",
    "CLAUDE_PRECOMPACT_COOLDOWN_S (P1) integer seconds — cooldown for repeated PreCompact decision:block emissions in save-progress-before-compact.sh. Default 90. Floor 30 (values below silently clamped). 0 disables (legacy — every block fires). Cooldown stamp at .claude/workflow-state/.precompact-last-block; reset on fresh .iteration-in-flight mtime so each new review iteration gets its own first block. Audit ref: .claude/prompts/workflow-hook-loop-audit.md § P1."
  ],
  "env": {
    "GIT_STRIP_CO_AUTHOR": "false",
    "_CLAUDE_HANDOFF_VALIDATION_MODE": "strict",
    "_CLAUDE_VERDICT_VALIDATION_MODE": "strict",
    "_CLAUDE_ISSUE_ID_VALIDATION_MODE": "strict",
    "_CLAUDE_PROJECT_KNOWLEDGE_MODE": "strict",
    "_CLAUDE_PK_PATH_MODE": "strict",
    "ENABLE_PROMPT_CACHING_1H": "1",
    "_FORCE_PROMPT_CACHING_5M": "1",
    "_CLAUDE_DELTA_REVIEW_MODE": "warn",
    "_CLAUDE_CAVEMAN_MODE": "lite",
    "CLAUDE_ISSUE_ID_NORMALIZE_VERSION": "2",
    "CLAUDE_VERDICT_BLOCK_TTL_HOURS": "6",
    "_CLAUDE_PRECOMPACT_COOLDOWN_S": "90"
  },
  "_permissions_comment": [
    "Recommended starter permissions for an uninterrupted /workflow run WITHOUT --dangerously-skip-permissions. These mirror settings.local.json.default (the install source) verbatim.",
    "Semantics (code.claude.com/docs/en/permissions): rules are evaluated deny -> ask -> allow; first match wins; deny always takes precedence. Rule strings use the SPACE-form 'Bash(rm -rf *)' — the form Claude Code itself writes on 'Yes, don't ask again'. The ':*' colon-form is equivalent ONLY as a trailing wildcard; a mid-pattern colon is treated literally.",
    "allow: language-agnostic core only — file edits (Edit/Write/TodoWrite), git write ops, safe filesystem writes, and rg/sed/awk/sort. Read-only commands (ls, cat, grep, find, head, tail, wc, echo, diff, and read-only git) are ALREADY free in every mode and are intentionally NOT listed. Build/test runners are language-specific — copy the matching _permissions_allow_templates_* line below into the allow array for your stack.",
    "deny: best-effort safety baseline (rm -rf and variants, git reset --hard, git clean, git checkout ., git restore ., git push --force/-f, sudo, chmod 777, dd, mkfs, truncate, shred, find -exec/-delete) plus secret reads (.env, .env.local, .env.*.local, secrets/**, ssh private keys). .env.example and .env.sample stay READABLE by design — there is intentionally no broad Read(.env.*) rule.",
    "LIMITS (docs): argument-scoped Bash deny rules are best-effort and bypassable via protocol swap, shell variables, subshells, or compound commands. deny rules do NOT fire in bypassPermissions / --dangerously-skip-permissions (only Claude Code's built-in rm -rf / and rm -rf ~ circuit breaker remains). curl and wget are already deny-by-default in Claude Code's command blocklist. For a HARD boundary use OS-level sandboxing (code.claude.com/docs/en/sandboxing) plus PreToolUse hooks, not deny rules alone.",
    "MERGE on install.sh --update: USER VALUES WIN and permission ARRAYS ARE NOT UNIONED. A fresh install copies the .default block verbatim; on update it is added only if you have no 'permissions' key yet. If you already have permissions.allow or permissions.deny arrays, these defaults are SKIPPED for that array — add the rules you want manually, or re-copy from .default.",
    "Governed natively: edit these arrays or run /permissions. This is a recommended default that you own and can change — the kit never overrides it."
  ],
  "_permissions_allow_templates_node": "Node/TS: \"Bash(npm run *)\", \"Bash(npm test *)\", \"Bash(npm ci)\", \"Bash(pnpm *)\", \"Bash(yarn *)\"  (NOT npm install / npx — postinstall scripts + env-runner escape)",
  "_permissions_allow_templates_python": "Python: \"Bash(pytest *)\", \"Bash(python -m pytest *)\", \"Bash(ruff *)\", \"Bash(mypy *)\"",
  "_permissions_allow_templates_go": "Go: \"Bash(make *)\", \"Bash(go test *)\", \"Bash(go build *)\", \"Bash(go vet *)\", \"Bash(go fmt *)\", \"Bash(go mod *)\"",
  "_permissions_allow_templates_rust": "Rust: \"Bash(cargo test *)\", \"Bash(cargo build *)\", \"Bash(cargo check *)\", \"Bash(cargo clippy *)\"",
  "_permissions_allow_templates_java": "Java: \"Bash(mvn *)\", \"Bash(gradle *)\", \"Bash(./gradlew *)\"",
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Edit",
      "Write",
      "TodoWrite",
      "Bash(git add *)",
      "Bash(git commit *)",
      "Bash(git checkout -b *)",
      "Bash(git switch *)",
      "Bash(git stash *)",
      "Bash(git worktree *)",
      "Bash(mkdir *)",
      "Bash(touch *)",
      "Bash(cp *)",
      "Bash(mv *)",
      "Bash(rg *)",
      "Bash(sed *)",
      "Bash(awk *)",
      "Bash(sort *)"
    ],
    "deny": [
      "Bash(rm -rf *)",
      "Bash(rm -fr *)",
      "Bash(rm -rf /)",
      "Bash(rm -rf ~)",
      "Bash(rm -rf ~/*)",
      "Bash(git reset --hard *)",
      "Bash(git clean *)",
      "Bash(git checkout .)",
      "Bash(git restore .)",
      "Bash(git push --force *)",
      "Bash(git push -f *)",
      "Bash(sudo *)",
      "Bash(chmod 777 *)",
      "Bash(chmod -R 777 *)",
      "Bash(chmod 0777 *)",
      "Bash(dd if=*)",
      "Bash(mkfs.*)",
      "Bash(truncate *)",
      "Bash(shred *)",
      "Bash(find * -exec *)",
      "Bash(find * -delete)",
      "Read(.env)",
      "Read(.env.local)",
      "Read(.env.*.local)",
      "Read(secrets/**)",
      "Read(**/.ssh/id_*)"
    ]
  },
  "_worktree_comment": "Uncomment for monorepos (100k+ files) to speed up code-reviewer worktree creation. Only checked-out paths will be visible to the reviewer agent. The kit ships Go-shaped defaults; for non-Go projects, replace the sparsePaths array with one of the language-specific templates below.",
  "_worktree_templates_python": "Python (Django / FastAPI / Flask): [\"src/\", \"tests/\", \"pyproject.toml\", \"requirements.txt\", \"setup.py\"]",
  "_worktree_templates_typescript": "TypeScript / Node.js: [\"src/\", \"tests/\", \"package.json\", \"tsconfig.json\"]",
  "_worktree_templates_rust": "Rust: [\"src/\", \"tests/\", \"Cargo.toml\", \"Cargo.lock\"]",
  "_worktree_templates_java": "Java (Maven / Gradle): [\"src/main/\", \"src/test/\", \"pom.xml\", \"build.gradle\", \"build.gradle.kts\"]",
  "worktree": {
    "sparsePaths": ["internal/", "cmd/", "go.mod", "go.sum", "Makefile"]
  }
}
